          "commentType": "FUNCTION",
          "texts": [
            {
              "value": "Inhibitor of serine proteases. Its primary target is elastase, but it also has a moderate affinity for plasmin and thrombin. Irreversibly inhibits trypsin, chymotrypsin and plasminogen activator. The aberrant form inhibits insulin-induced NO synthesis in platelets, decreases coagulation time and has proteolytic activity against insulin and plasmin"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "commentType": "FUNCTION",
          "molecule": "Short peptide from AAT",
          "texts": [
            {
              "value": "Reversible chymotrypsin inhibitor. It also inhibits elastase, but not trypsin. Its major physiological function is the protection of the lower respiratory tract against proteolytic destruction by human leukocyte elastase (HLE)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "commentType": "SUBCELLULAR LOCATION",
          "note": {
            "texts": [
              {
                "value": "The S and Z allele are not secreted effectively and accumulate intracellularly in the endoplasmic reticulum"
